    "rai:dataLimitations": "The 80-question item count limits statistical power for fine-grained model comparisons. Contamination risk is non-trivial for newer models since GPQA has been public since 2023. The difficulty labels are cohort-dependent, which reflect failure rates on our specific ten-model open-weight cohort and may shift for models of different architectures or training distributions. Completion-rate variability on the Kaggle platform means some per-model per-task cells are missing (see run_metadata.csv for the full completion picture). Task 10 (DPP Sequence) has near-universal context-length failures (22 of 23 models truncated) and should be treated as preliminary.",
    "rai:dataBiases": "Models evaluated are those available on the Kaggle Benchmarks platform as of early 2026; the cohort is not a representative sample of all LLMs and skews toward larger, API-accessible frontier and mid-tier systems. The question set inherits any biases present in GPQA Diamond (graduate-science bias toward physics, chemistry, and biology). In terms of language, the dataset is in English only.",
    "rai:personalSensitiveInformation": "None. The dataset contains graduate-level science questions from GPQA Diamond (a published educational assessment) and language model outputs on those questions. No personal data of any kind is included.",
    "rai:dataUseCases": "Intended for evaluation-methodology research on LLM metacognition: comparing declarative calibration metrics (ECE, Brier) against behavioral routing metrics (Delegation AUC-ROC) on matched item sets; studying cross-task dissociation patterns within a single model; sensitivity analysis of reward schedules and difficulty thresholds; developing selective-prediction system; and evaluating routing policy.",
    "rai:dataSocialImpact": "The benchmark supports evaluation of whether language models can act on their uncertainty rather than merely report it, which is relevant to safer routing, triage, and human-AI collaboration. The evaluation methodology is expected to have neutral-to-positive societal impact by improving the precision of claims about model metacognitive competence.",
    "rai:hasSyntheticData": false,
    "prov:wasDerivedFrom": "https://huggingface.co/datasets/fingertap/GPQA-Diamond",
    "prov:wasGeneratedBy": "This dataset of 80 questions are extracted from the GPQA Diamond dataset. First, the empirical per-question difficulty is computed by running 10 open-weight models on the full 198-question set and defining difficulty as the fraction of models that answered incorrectly. Then, from this distribution, 80 questions are eventually selected spanning difficulty 0.44-0.89 to maximize meaningful delegation variance. Questions below 0.44 are too easy (most models answer correctly, so delegation is rarely warranted) and above 0.89 are too hard (most models fail regardless)",

